# /boot/firmware/config.txt notes for the wall display Pi.
#
# gpu_mem IS LEFT AT THE DEFAULT (76). An earlier version of this file recommended gpu_mem=256 to
# fix hardware decode; that recommendation is WITHDRAWN, for two reasons found on 2026-08-18:
#
# 1. HARDWARE DECODE IS NOW DELIBERATELY DISABLED (see kiosk.service). Five simultaneous H.264
#    sessions on the Pi 4's single decoder produced ~15 visible ~1s skips per 4 minutes; software
#    decode produced zero, and used slightly LESS CPU. So the decoder is not wanted at all.
#
# 2. THE 76MB FAILURE WAS PROBABLY A LEAK, NOT A SHORTAGE. With gpu_mem back at 76 and a fresh
#    boot, hardware decode worked fine -- the same 76MB that had been failing. The original
#    failures began 19 minutes after boot, after several kiosk restarts:
#
#      bcm2835_mmal_vchiq: failed to create component -62 (Not enough GPU mem?)
#
#    which points at decode components not being released across restarts, with gpu_mem=256 merely
#    postponing exhaustion. Moot now that the decoder is unused, but do not treat 256 as the fix if
#    hardware decode is ever revisited.
#
# Leaving gpu_mem at 76 returns ~180MB of RAM to the system.
